To achieve a layout where key-value pairs flow into multiple columns, you can use CSS columns. Here's how you can set it up:

```css
.key-value-table {
  column-count: auto; /* Adjusts based on screen width */
  column-gap: 20px; /* Space between columns */
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.key-value-pair {
  margin-bottom: 10px; /* Space between pairs */
}
```

This setup will create a responsive layout where the key-value pairs flow into as many columns as fit the screen width, maintaining their order.
